---
/*
  /lab/dark/ — Second Iteration, dark palette copy-base.

  The seven content blocks B1–B7 (technical-editing.md §5) rendered on a DARK
  palette with heavy combination variety, per iteration-2-notes.md. This is the
  "Black palette (new)" base plus the reverses/mixes Andrew asked for — an
  exploration page whose job is to make variety *perceptible*.

  Grounds alternate two dark surfaces: near-black (~#141412) and dark-blue
  (~#0E1A2B / #10162B). Text is ivory (~#F4F1EA); the single voltage accent is
  orange (~#E4632A / #D2691E). Two blocks INVERT (a light ivory block/band sitting
  on the dark page) and read as the reverse of the dark cards.

  §4 block-combination catalog deployed across the seven:
    - B1  double-outline (2×1px, ~5px apart, solid fill) on an orange↔near-black
          gradient ground  → double-outline + solid-inside/gradient-outside
    - B2  full-bleed dark-blue BAND, hairline-ruled list, no card → band (vs B1 card)
    - B3  INVERSE light ivory CARD on the near-black page (dark-on-light) → inverse
    - B4  accent-tint COLOR BLOCKS (orange-tint stat cards) on a blue↔near-black
          gradient ground → color block + solid-inside/gradient-outside
    - B5  doc-excerpt in a double-outline near-black frame on a deepening ground
    - B6  INVERSE light ivory BAND (full-bleed) → reverse of B3's card, band vs card
    - B7  statement in a double-outline card on a focal (amplify-toward-dark)
          gradient ground → solid-inside/gradient-outside close

  GRADIENT RULE (iteration-2-notes §4 / technical-editing §3): gradients are used
  more here but NEVER inside a lined/carded block. Every gradient lives on the
  section GROUND, outside the block; each block interior keeps a SOLID fill. The
  .grad-* classes are only ever applied to <section>, never to a .card/.dbl/.band.

  Fonts (NO ROBOTO). Pairings alternate and never repeat on consecutive blocks:
    B1 Fraunces + Newsreader · B2 Ubuntu Condensed + Hanken Grotesk ·
    B3 Cuprum + Spectral · B4 Chakra Petch + Source Serif 4 (Space Mono figures) ·
    B5 Oxanium + Hanken Grotesk (Space Mono excerpt) · B6 Cuprum italic + Newsreader ·
    B7 Nova Square (sparingly) + Source Serif 4.

  Type is up: body 20–21px / 1.6, measures 74–84ch, headlines 32–46 varying size
  AND color (some ivory, some orange, some inverted). Every block closes with an
  italic muted caption in its own font, leading with a plain-language Feel:.

  Own shell — no BaseLayout. Static. Content verbatim from technical-editing.md §5.
  B3 CTA → /varpage/teardown/.
*/
import LabMenu from '../../components/LabMenu.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>/lab/dark — dark palette copy-base (iteration 2)</title>
  <meta
    name="description"
    content="Dark palette copy-base: near-black and dark-blue grounds, ivory text, orange accent. Seven content blocks with heavy combination variety — double-outline, inverse, color-block, band vs card, solid-inside/gradient-outside."
  />

  <!-- Fonts via Google Fonts. No Roboto anywhere.
       Headings: Fraunces, Ubuntu Condensed, Cuprum, Chakra Petch, Oxanium, Nova Square.
       Body: Newsreader, Hanken Grotesk, Spectral, Source Serif 4, Space Mono (mono/excerpt). -->
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link
    href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Chakra+Petch:wght@400;500;600&family=Cuprum:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400;1,700&family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,500&family=Hanken+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600&family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;1,6..72,400&family=Nova+Square&family=Oxanium:wght@400;600;700&family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,400;0,8..60,600;1,8..60,400&family=Space+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=Spectral:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;1,400&family=Ubuntu+Condensed&display=swap"
    rel="stylesheet"
  />

  <style is:global>
    :root {
      /* Dark palette grounds (iteration-2-notes.md §6). */
      --nearblack:      #141412;   /* near-black ground */
      --nearblack-deep: #0C0C0A;   /* deeper end for focal / gradient stops */
      --nearblack-lift: #1C1B18;   /* card fill on near-black sections (solid) */
      --blue:           #0E1A2B;   /* dark-blue ground */
      --blue-2:         #10162B;   /* alternate dark-blue */
      --blue-deep:      #091320;   /* deeper end for gradient stops */
      --blue-lift:      #16273D;   /* card fill on dark-blue sections (solid) */

      /* Ivory text + the inverse (light-on-dark-page) surfaces. */
      --ivory:      #F4F1EA;                    /* primary text on dark */
      --ivory-soft: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.72);  /* secondary text */
      --ivory-mute: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.56);  /* captions / notes */
      --inv-bg:     #F4F1EA;   /* inverse block ground (light on dark page) */
      --inv-bg-2:   #EDE8DD;   /* inverse secondary fill */
      --inv-ink:    #17140E;   /* warm near-black ink for inverse blocks */
      --inv-soft:   rgba(23, 20, 14, 0.66);
      --inv-mute:   rgba(23, 20, 14, 0.55);

      /* Single voltage accent — orange. */
      --orange:      #E4632A;
      --orange-2:    #D2691E;
      --orange-deep: #B44E1F;
      --orange-tint: #E96A2E;   /* accent-tint color-block fill (B4) */

      /* Hairlines on dark. */
      --line:      rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.16);
      --line-soft: rgba(244, 241, 234, 0.10);
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html { -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--nearblack);
      color: var(--ivory);
      /* Default body face (overridden per block) — never Roboto. */
      font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
      text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
    }

    .page { display: block; }

    /* One block = one section. Generous padding for the exploration. */
    .blk { padding: 6rem 1.5rem; }
    .ground-nearblack { background: var(--nearblack); }
    .ground-blue      { background: var(--blue); }

    /* Wider measures per iteration 2 — no skinny 62ch columns. */
    .col      { max-width: 78ch; margin-inline: auto; }
    .col-wide { max-width: 84ch; margin-inline: auto; }
    .col-lead { max-width: 74ch; margin-inline: auto; }

    /* ---- Gradient grounds. Applied ONLY to <section>, NEVER to a lined/carded
       block. The block interior always keeps a solid fill. Soft but present,
       carrying color (orange↔near-black, blue↔near-black). ---- */
    .grad-orange { background: linear-gradient(168deg, var(--orange-deep) 0%, var(--nearblack) 46%, var(--nearblack-deep) 100%); }
    .grad-blue   { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--blue-deep) 0%, var(--blue) 55%, #0B1B2E 100%); }
    .grad-deepen { background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--nearblack) 0%, var(--nearblack-deep) 100%); }
    .grad-focus  { background: radial-gradient(120% 120% at 50% 0%, var(--nearblack) 0%, var(--nearblack-deep) 78%); }

    /* ---- Double-outline: two thin borders ~5px apart, solid fill throughout.
       Padding between the outer and inner border shows the SAME solid fill, so
       it reads as two close lines around a solid block — no gradient inside. ---- */
    .dbl {
      background: var(--nearblack-lift);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 5px;
    }
    .dbl > .dbl-in {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 9px;
      padding: 2.5rem 2.25rem;
      background: var(--nearblack-lift);
    }
    .dbl--accent { border-color: rgba(228, 99, 42, 0.55); }
    .dbl--accent > .dbl-in { border-color: rgba(228, 99, 42, 0.40); }

    /* ---- Single carved card (solid). ---- */
    .card {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 2.5rem 2.25rem;
    }

    a { color: var(--orange); text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
    a:hover { color: var(--orange-2); }

    /* Captions — italic, muted, in the block's own font, ≤17. Lead with Feel:. */
    .cap { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--ivory-mute); margin-top: 1.9rem; font-style: italic; }
    .cap b { font-style: italic; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ivory-soft); }

    /* =====================================================================
       B1 — premise (prose) · Stripe Press
       Fraunces heading (ORANGE) + Newsreader body · double-outline card on an
       orange↔near-black gradient ground. Solid inside, gradient outside.
       ===================================================================== */
    .b1-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Fraunces', serif;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 15px;
      letter-spacing: 0.14em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--orange);
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .b1-body {
      font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 21px;
      line-height: 1.62;
      color: var(--ivory);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .b1-cap { font-family: 'Fraunces', serif; }

    /* =====================================================================
       B2 — palette + surface (rhythm list) · Linear
       Ubuntu Condensed heading (IVORY, large) + Hanken Grotesk items ·
       full-bleed dark-blue BAND, hairline-ruled, NO card. Band vs B1's card.
       ===================================================================== */
    .b2-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 14px;
      letter-spacing: 0.42px;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--orange);
      margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    }
    .b2-head {
      font-family: 'Ubuntu Condensed', sans-serif;
      font-size: 44px;
      line-height: 1.08;
      letter-spacing: -0.022em;
      color: var(--ivory);
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
    }
    .b2-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .b2-list li {
      font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--ivory-soft);
      padding-block: 1.15rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line-soft);
    }
    .b2-list li:first-child { border-top: none; }
    .b2-list li b { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ivory); }
    .b2-cap { font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif; }

    /* =====================================================================
       B3 — long-text handling (list) + CTA · 37signals/Basecamp
       INVERSE: light ivory CARD on the near-black page — dark-on-light.
       Cuprum heading (near-black) + Spectral reading + one orange CTA.
       ===================================================================== */
    .inv-card {
      background: var(--inv-bg);
      color: var(--inv-ink);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 3rem 2.5rem;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px rgba(23, 20, 14, 0.10);
    }
    .b3-head {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 38px;
      line-height: 1.12;
      color: var(--inv-ink);
      margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
    }
    .b3-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 2.2rem; }
    .b3-list li {
      font-family: 'Spectral', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.62;
      color: var(--inv-soft);
      margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    }
    .b3-list li b { font-weight: 600; color: var(--inv-ink); }
    .b3-cta { margin-top: 0.5rem; }
    .b3-btn {
      display: inline-block;
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 20px;
      letter-spacing: 0.01em;
      background: var(--orange);
      color: var(--ivory);
      padding: 0.75rem 1.5rem;
      border-radius: 10px;
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .b3-btn:hover { background: var(--orange-deep); color: var(--ivory); }
    .b3-cap { font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif; color: var(--inv-mute); }

    /* =====================================================================
       B4 — block rhythm and sequencing (stat-dense) · Stripe
       Chakra Petch heading + Source Serif 4 body + Space Mono figures ·
       accent-tint COLOR BLOCKS (orange stat cards, contrasting near-black text)
       on a blue↔near-black gradient ground. Solid inside, gradient outside.
       ===================================================================== */
    .b4-eyebrow {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-size: 14px;
      letter-spacing: 0.02em;
      color: var(--ivory-mute);
      margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
    }
    .b4-head {
      font-family: 'Chakra Petch', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 34px;
      line-height: 1.14;
      color: var(--ivory);
      margin: 0 0 1.8rem;
    }
    .b4-grid { display: grid; gap: 1.15rem; }
    /* Accent-tint color block: filled orange, contrasting text. Solid fill. */
    .b4-stat {
      background: var(--orange-tint);
      color: var(--nearblack-deep);
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 1.75rem 1.9rem;
    }
    .b4-fig {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 26px;
      line-height: 1.2;
      color: var(--nearblack-deep);
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    }
    .b4-src {
      font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.55;
      color: rgba(12, 12, 10, 0.86);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .b4-cap { font-family: 'Space Mono', monospace; }

    /* =====================================================================
       B5 — bare imagery (bare frame / doc-excerpt) · Stripe
       Oxanium heading (ORANGE) + Hanken Grotesk body + Space Mono excerpt ·
       double-outline near-black frame on a deepening near-black gradient ground.
       ===================================================================== */
    .b5-head {
      font-family: 'Oxanium', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 34px;
      line-height: 1.14;
      color: var(--orange);
      margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
    }
    .b5-body {
      font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 20px;
      line-height: 1.6;
      color: var(--ivory-soft);
      margin: 0 0 2rem;
    }
    .bare { margin: 0; }
    .doc-excerpt {
      font-family: 'Space Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
      font-size: 16px;
      line-height: 1.75;
      color: var(--ivory-soft);
      background: var(--nearblack-deep);
      white-space: pre-wrap;
      overflow-x: auto;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .doc-excerpt .anno { color: var(--orange); }
    .b5-figcap {
      font-family: 'Hanken Grotesk', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 16px;
      color: var(--ivory-mute);
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }
    .b5-cap { font-family: 'Oxanium', system-ui, sans-serif; }

    /* =====================================================================
       B6 — the 2026 warning (sidenote) · Works in Progress
       INVERSE light ivory BAND (full-bleed) — reverse of B3's inverse card.
       Cuprum italic heading + Newsreader body + a margin note.
       ===================================================================== */
    .b6-band {
      background: var(--inv-bg);
      color: var(--inv-ink);
    }
    .b6-head {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-style: italic;
      font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 36px;
      line-height: 1.14;
      color: var(--inv-ink);
      margin: 0 0 1.8rem;
    }
    .b6-wrap { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 74ch) 16rem; gap: 2.75rem; align-items: start; }
    .b6-body {
      font-family: 'Newsreader', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 21px;
      line-height: 1.62;
      color: var(--inv-soft);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .b6-side {
      font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif;
      font-style: italic;
      font-size: 17px;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: var(--inv-mute);
      padding-top: 0.4rem;
    }
    .b6-cap { font-family: 'Cuprum', sans-serif; color: var(--inv-mute); }
    @media (max-width: 860px) {
      .b6-wrap { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .b6-side { border-left: 2px solid var(--orange); padding-left: 1rem; }
    }

    /* =====================================================================
       B7 — what to harvest (statement close) · Stripe Press
       Nova Square heading (used sparingly — the one statement) + Source Serif 4 ·
       double-outline card on a focal (amplify-toward-dark) gradient ground.
       ===================================================================== */
    .b7-head {
      font-family: 'Nova Square', system-ui, sans-serif;
      font-size: 40px;
      line-height: 1.12;
      letter-spacing: -0.01em;
      color: var(--orange);
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .b7-body {
      font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 21px;
      line-height: 1.62;
      color: var(--ivory);
      margin: 0;
    }
    .b7-body + .b7-body { margin-top: 1.1rem; }
    .b7-cap { font-family: 'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif; }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <LabMenu active="dark" />
  <main class="page">

    <!-- ============ B1 — premise (prose) ============ -->
    <!-- template: prose · treatment: double-outline card + solid-inside/gradient-outside (orange↔near-black) -->
    <section class="blk grad-orange">
      <div class="col-lead">
        <div class="dbl dbl--accent">
          <div class="dbl-in">
            <p class="b1-eyebrow">Premise</p>
            <p class="b1-body">Your premise holds. A live site is a better template source than a template marketplace, because you can read the decisions rather than inherit someone's content model. And the reskin is only about six variables: neutral ramp, one accent, radius scale, spacing scale, text measure, border weight. Fix those six and any layout you admire becomes yours.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="cap b1-cap"><b>Feel:</b> warm, editorial, deliberate. Fraunces eyebrow + Newsreader body 21/1.62 · 74ch · double-outline card (2×1px, ~5px apart, solid near-black fill) on an orange↔near-black gradient ground · orange accent — similar to Stripe Press.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B2 — palette + surface (rhythm list) ============ -->
    <!-- template: rhythm-list · treatment: Linear — full-bleed dark-blue band (no card) -->
    <section class="blk ground-blue">
      <div class="col-wide">
        <p class="b2-eyebrow">Palette + surface</p>
        <h2 class="b2-head">The white-main systems worth copying wholesale</h2>
        <ul class="b2-list">
          <li><b>Mercury</b> — the reference for premium-restrained off-white. Near-invisible borders, almost no shadow, one accent used sparingly. Serious without being cold, which is your construction-buyer problem exactly.</li>
          <li><b>Anthropic</b> — warm ivory ground, serif headings, very low saturation. Closest live example of your §1 brief: calm enough to read as a default rather than a pitch.</li>
          <li><b>Attio</b> — white, precise, tight grid. Shows how far a single accent goes when everything else is neutral.</li>
          <li><b>Notion</b> — the smoothed-edges reference. Radius scale, soft card fills, warm white. Study it for where rounding stops; over-rounding is what makes a premium site read as a toy.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="cap b2-cap"><b>Feel:</b> crisp, structural, precise. Ubuntu Condensed head 44 (−.022em) + Hanken Grotesk items 20/1.6 · 84ch · full-bleed dark-blue band, hairline rules, no card · orange eyebrow — similar to Linear.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B3 — long-text handling (list) + CTA ============ -->
    <!-- template: prose-list + plain-cta · treatment: 37signals — INVERSE light card (dark-on-light) on the near-black page -->
    <section class="blk ground-nearblack">
      <div class="col">
        <div class="inv-card">
          <h2 class="b3-head">Long-text handling</h2>
          <ul class="b3-list">
            <li><b>Stripe Press</b> — book typography on the web. Measure control, no chrome, headings that hold their own without decoration.</li>
            <li><b>Works in Progress</b> — sidenotes, footnotes, sustained reading. Relevant to your Notion-docs layer and the sample teardowns.</li>
            <li><b>37signals / Basecamp</b> — plain speech, opinionated blocks, one CTA, active refusal of decoration. The nearest ethos match to your §6 and §9.</li>
          </ul>
          <div class="b3-cta">
            <a class="b3-btn" href="/varpage/teardown/">Request a free teardown &rarr;</a>
          </div>
          <p class="cap b3-cap"><b>Feel:</b> plain-spoken, high-contrast, reversed. Cuprum head 38 + Spectral reading 20/1.62, one orange CTA · 78ch · inverse light ivory card (dark-on-light) on the near-black page · orange accent — similar to 37signals / Basecamp.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B4 — block rhythm and sequencing (stat-dense) ============ -->
    <!-- template: stat-dense · treatment: Stripe — accent-tint color blocks + solid-inside/gradient-outside (blue↔near-black) -->
    <section class="blk grad-blue">
      <div class="col">
        <p class="b4-eyebrow">// block rhythm and sequencing — big SaaS</p>
        <h2 class="b4-head">Sequencing density so it reads light</h2>
        <div class="b4-grid">
          <div class="b4-stat">
            <div class="b4-fig">Linear</div>
            <p class="b4-src">take the spacing rhythm and the restraint, invert the palette. The lesson is vertical rhythm, and whitespace used structurally.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="b4-stat">
            <div class="b4-fig">Stripe</div>
            <p class="b4-src">how to sequence dense information so density stops feeling heavy. Useful for your §5, where you have a statistic plus a source plus a caveat in one block.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="cap b4-cap"><b>Feel:</b> dense but voltaic, engineered. Chakra Petch head 34 + Source Serif 4 source 20/1.55, Space Mono figures · 78ch · accent-tint color blocks (solid orange fill, near-black text) on a blue↔near-black gradient ground · orange accent — similar to Stripe.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B5 — bare imagery (bare frame / doc-excerpt) ============ -->
    <!-- template: bare-frame · treatment: Stripe — double-outline near-black frame on a deepening ground -->
    <section class="blk grad-deepen">
      <div class="col">
        <h2 class="b5-head">Bare imagery</h2>
        <p class="b5-body">Mercury, Ramp, and Arc all show images without device frames, drop shadows, or perspective tilt. That is the current premium signal, and it happens to be the only image treatment that fits you.</p>
        <figure class="bare">
          <div class="dbl">
            <div class="dbl-in" style="padding:1.75rem;background:var(--nearblack-deep);">
              <pre class="doc-excerpt"><span class="anno"># teardown — annotation layer</span>
&gt; hero      no device frame · no shadow · no tilt
&gt; measure   78ch
&gt; radius    12px
&gt; border    double-outline (2×1px)
&gt; accent    orange · one per block
<span class="anno">&gt; note      the artifact IS the image</span></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="b5-figcap">Bare frame stands in for the image: a monospace document excerpt, no chrome.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p class="cap b5-cap"><b>Feel:</b> technical, document-like, dim-lit. Oxanium head 34 + Hanken Grotesk body 20/1.6 + Space Mono excerpt 16 · 78ch · double-outline near-black frame (solid fill) on a deepening near-black gradient ground · orange accent — similar to Stripe.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ============ B6 — the 2026 warning (sidenote) ============ -->
